{"title":"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 25","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Formula_of_tanx)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Formula of tanx)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(2_minutes,_easy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (2 minutes, easy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There is a unique sequence of integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/b/95b332fa3520bc51759c2597459864c5d8be0909.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, \\cdots a_{2023}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"13\" /> such that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/4/0c431ac36edd847d292077bee7205bbf3f2c3649.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\tan2023x = \\frac{a_1 \\tan x + a_3 \\tan^3 x + a_5 \\tan^5 x + \\cdots + a_{2023} \\tan^{2023} x}{1 + a_2 \\tan^2 x + a_4 \\tan^4 x \\cdots + a_{2022} \\tan^{2022} x}\\]\" width=\"514\" height=\"42\" />whenever <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/4/d640e62682ee0b0fdd7953f0217d2cb2a97e416f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan 2023x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"78\" height=\"14\" /> is defined. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/7/34732a591951bdeb9ec47ab226976e9ff3d60f2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2023}?$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/5/1056b523fc5aa922a674cbceab742c10abcdd8f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } -2023 \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } -2022 \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } -1 \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } 1 \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } 2023$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"504\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/5/585725b70265e24ce5228a8d756dd3769333aa9d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\cos 2023 x + i \\sin 2023 x &amp;= (\\cos x + i \\sin x)^{2023}\\\\ &amp;= \\cos^{2023} x + \\binom{2023}{1} \\cos^{2022} x (i\\sin x) + \\binom{2023}{2} \\cos^{2021} x (i \\sin x)^{2} +\\binom{2023}{3} \\cos^{2020} x (i \\sin x)^{3}\\\\ &amp;+ \\dots + \\binom{2023}{2022} \\cos x (i \\sin x)^{2022} + (i \\sin x)^{2023}\\\\ &amp;= \\cos^{2023} x + i \\binom{2023}{1} \\cos^{2022} x \\sin x - \\binom{2023}{2} \\cos^{2021} x \\sin^{2} x - i\\binom{2023}{3} \\cos^{2020} x \\sin^{3} x + \\dots\\\\ &amp;- \\binom{2023}{2022} \\cos x \\sin^{2022} x - i \\sin^{2023} x\\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"922\" height=\"261\" />\n</p><p>By equating real and imaginary parts:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/0/560853fd66769364759b09232bb4b348e9f4f2dc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos 2023 x = \\cos^{2023} x - \\binom{2023}{2} \\cos^{2021} x \\sin^{2} x + \\dots - \\binom{2023}{2022} \\cos x \\sin^{2022} x\\]\" width=\"576\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/a/f7a6d4d85f661be5a354a8b14acf1e8055a72c84.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin 2023 x = \\binom{2023}{1} \\cos^{2022} x \\sin x - \\binom{2023}{3} \\cos^{2020} x \\sin^{3} x + \\dots - \\sin^{2023} x\\]\" width=\"572\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/b/6cb1333f2842c86b8a0558e640dc1b34aa0a43e2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\tan2023x  &amp;= \\frac{ \\sin2023x }{ \\cos2023x } = \\frac{ \\binom{2023}{1} \\cos^{2022} x \\sin x - \\binom{2023}{3} \\cos^{2020} x \\sin^{3} x + \\dots - \\sin^{2023} x }{ \\cos^{2023} x - \\binom{2023}{2} \\cos^{2021} x \\sin^{2} x + \\dots - \\binom{2023}{2022} \\cos x \\sin^{2022} x }\\\\ &amp;= \\frac{ \\binom{2023}{1} \\frac{\\cos^{2022} x \\sin x}{\\cos^{2023} x} - \\binom{2023}{3} \\frac{\\cos^{2020} x \\sin^{3} x}{\\cos^{2023} x} + \\dots - \\frac{\\sin^{2023} x}{\\cos^{2023} x} }{ \\frac{\\cos^{2023} x}{\\cos^{2023} x} - \\binom{2023}{2} \\frac{\\cos^{2021} x \\sin^{2} x}{\\cos^{2023} x} + \\dots - \\binom{2023}{2022} \\frac{\\cos x \\sin^{2022} x}{\\cos^{2023} x}  }\\\\ &amp;= \\frac{ \\binom{2023}{1} \\tan x - \\binom{2023}{3} \\tan^{3}x + \\dots - \\tan^{2023}x }{ 1 - \\binom{2023}{2} \\tan^{2}x + \\dots - \\binom{2023}{2022} \\tan^{2022} x }\\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"664\" height=\"162\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/3/3532c241bd86352a92f8563fe965756dcb792f86.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_{2023} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}-1}\\]\" width=\"132\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>This problem is the same as problem 7.64 in the Art of Problem Solving textbook Precalculus chapter 7 that asks to prove <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/5/f952d9d3465f9a730c75a9042b430edd2f016ad0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan{nx} = \\frac{\\binom{n}{1}\\tan{x} - \\binom{n}{3}\\tan^{3}{x} + \\binom{n}{5}\\tan^{5}{x} - \\binom{n}{7}\\tan^{7}{x} + \\dots}{1 - \\binom{n}{2}\\tan^{2}{x} + \\binom{n}{4}\\tan^{4}{x}  - \\binom{n}{6}\\tan^{6}{x} + \\dots}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"482\" height=\"50\" />\n</p><p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Isabelchen\">isabelchen</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Formula_of_tanx.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Formula_of_tanx)\">Solution 2 (Formula of tanx)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Formula of tanx)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/7/be704d141dc71f62c41abb04ae4980ab6f0bd430.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan{kx} = \\frac{\\binom{k}{1}\\tan{x} - \\binom{k}{3}\\tan^{3}{x} + \\cdots \\pm \\binom{k}{k}\\tan^{k}{x}}{\\binom{k}{0}\\tan^{0}{x} - \\binom{k}{2}\\tan^{2}{x} + \\cdots \\pm \\binom{k}{k-1}\\tan^{k-1}{x}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"424\" height=\"53\" />, where k is odd and the sign of each term alternates between positive and negative. To realize this during the test, you should know the formulas of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/e/77edaa5999897c1c726d71888dd93e349361e0a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan{2x}, \\tan{3x},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/e/ade5818b8b6148d437bbbd48bbea475e5a907563.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan{4x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />, and can notice the pattern from that. The expression given essentially matches the formula of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/5/a2520e890a3728817d243703879f349e545f61ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan{kx}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" /> exactly. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/d/90df8247450411615166faea7e60906065bf88fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2023}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"13\" /> is evidently equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/c/80c37321e64e16ccec0f8ecb67c93307d177f1b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pm\\binom{2023}{2023}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"80\" height=\"55\" />, or 1. However, it could be positive or negative. Notice that in the numerator, whenever the exponent of the tangent term is congruent to 1 mod 4, the term is positive. Whenever the exponent of the tangent term is 3 mod 4, the term is negative. 2023, which is assigned to k, is congruent to 3 mod 4. This means that the term of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/a/89ad7e65b4bb00269e80b8f263d7ada51a1435ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{k}{k}\\tan^{k}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"91\" height=\"55\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/d/23d30434ebf74e2513b0d0b631c4b004e75a3ec5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } -1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"79\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nNotice: If you have time and don't know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/a/41a615db25c2bdce149758fa06d41682738f19f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan{3x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/e/ade5818b8b6148d437bbbd48bbea475e5a907563.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan{4x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />, you'd have to keep deriving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/5/a2520e890a3728817d243703879f349e545f61ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan{kx}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" /> until you see the pattern.\n</p><p>~lprado\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For odd <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/3/b83b4e3c027f02283ed1f6baa572b618ef7c23f8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\tan nx &amp; = \\frac{\\sin nx}{\\cos nx} \\\\ &amp; = \\frac{\\frac{1}{2i} \\left( e^{i n x} - e^{-i n x} \\right)} {\\frac{1}{2} \\left( e^{i n x} + e^{-i n x} \\right)} \\\\ &amp; = - i \\frac{e^{i n x} - e^{-i n x}}{e^{i n x} + e^{-i n x}} \\\\ &amp; = - i  \\frac{\\left( \\cos x + i \\sin x \\right)^n - \\left( \\cos x - i \\sin x \\right)^n} {\\left( \\cos x + i \\sin x \\right)^n + \\left( \\cos x - i \\sin x \\right)^n} \\\\ &amp; = \\frac{ - 2 i \\sum_{m=0}^{(n-1)/2} \\binom{n}{2m + 1} \\left( \\cos x \\right)^{n - 2m - 1} \\left( i \\sin x \\right)^{2m + 1}} {2 \\sum_{m=0}^{(n-1)/2} \\binom{n}{2m} \\left( \\cos x \\right)^{n - 2m} \\left( i \\sin x \\right)^{2m}} \\\\ &amp; = \\frac{ \\frac{1}{\\left( \\cos x \\right)^n} \\sum_{m=0}^{(n-1)/2} \\binom{n}{2m + 1} \\left( \\cos x \\right)^{n - 2m - 1} \\left( i \\sin x \\right)^{2m + 1}} {i \\frac{1}{\\left( \\cos x \\right)^n} \\sum_{m=0}^{(n-1)/2} \\binom{n}{2m} \\left( \\cos x \\right)^{n - 2m} \\left( i \\sin x \\right)^{2m}} \\\\ &amp; = \\frac{ \\sum_{m=0}^{(n-1)/2} \\binom{n}{2m + 1} \\left( i \\tan x \\right)^{2m + 1}} {i \\sum_{m=0}^{(n-1)/2} \\binom{n}{2m} \\left( i \\tan x \\right)^{2m}} \\\\ &amp; = \\frac{ \\sum_{m=0}^{(n-1)/2} \\binom{n}{2m + 1} \\left( \\tan x \\right)^{2m + 1} i^{2m + 1}} {\\sum_{m=0}^{(n-1)/2} \\binom{n}{2m} \\left( \\tan x \\right)^{2m} i^{2m + 1}} \\\\ &amp; = \\frac{ \\sum_{m=0}^{(n-1)/2} \\binom{n}{2m + 1} \\left( \\tan x \\right)^{2m + 1} \\left( -1 \\right)^m} {\\sum_{m=0}^{(n-1)/2} \\binom{n}{2m} \\left( \\tan x \\right)^{2m} \\left( -1 \\right)^m}  . \\end{align*}\" width=\"461\" height=\"500\" />\n</p><p>Thus, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/3/a43199f5e00da9f32f54473be6c06201c0b7096d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 2023$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26e73f4cd5651fb76aef73e1b9783fcfea57287c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} a_{2023} &amp; = \\binom{2023}{2023} \\left( -1 \\right)^{(2023-1)/2} \\\\ &amp; = \\left( -1 \\right)^{1011} \\\\ &amp; = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C) -1}}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"232\" height=\"118\" />\n</p><p>~Steven Chen (Professor Chen Education Palace, www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can use recursion to find a pattern for this problem. Notice that,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b312e710120be4eb4d8cee0040f782ce85aaca7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\tan x &amp;= \\tan x\\\\ \\tan 2x &amp;= \\dfrac{\\tan x + \\tan x}{1 - \\tan^2 x} = \\dfrac{2\\tan x}{1 - \\tan^2 x}\\\\ \\tan 3x &amp;= \\dfrac{\\tan 2x + \\tan x}{1 - \\tan 2x \\tan x} = \\dfrac{3\\tan x - \\tan^3 x}{1 - 3\\tan^2 x} \\end{align*}\" width=\"347\" height=\"109\" />\nThe coefficient of the highest degree term seems to be always <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/f/7cfbd35086ffefb83637d42166582b43c8a1ff4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pm 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" />. Now, we prove this by an imcomplete  mathematical induction.\n</p>\n<ul><li>Firstly, we suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is odd, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/f/7df52dc0b7697b91ec130f836bc17b79f0121a85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan nx = \\dfrac{a_1\\tan x + a_3\\tan^3 x + \\cdots + a_n\\tan^n x}{a_0 + a_2\\tan^2 x + \\cdots + a_{n - 1}\\tan^{n - 1} x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"366\" height=\"45\" />, then</li></ul>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/b/f6bbd6c803509af2938e7638b2ae0911b2c271b7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\tan(n + 1)x &amp;= \\dfrac{\\tan nx + \\tan x}{1 - \\tan nx \\tan x}\\\\ &amp;= \\dfrac{\\dfrac{a_1\\tan x + a_3\\tan^3 x + \\cdots + a_n\\tan^n x}{a_0 + a_2\\tan^2 x + \\cdots + a_{n - 1}\\tan^{n - 1} x} + \\tan x}{1 - \\dfrac{a_1\\tan x + a_3\\tan^3 x + \\cdots + a_n\\tan^n x}{a_0 + a_2\\tan^2 x + \\cdots + a_{n - 1}\\tan^{n - 1} x}\\tan x}\\\\ &amp;= \\dfrac{a_1\\tan x + a_3\\tan^3 x + \\cdots + a_n\\tan^n x + a_0\\tan x + a_2\\tan^3 x + \\cdots + a_{n - 1}\\tan^n x}{a_0 + a_2\\tan^2x + \\cdots + a_{n - 1}\\tan^{n - 1}x - a_1\\tan^2 x - a_3\\tan^4 x - \\cdots \\boxed{-a_n\\tan^{n + 1} x}} \\end{align*}\" width=\"734\" height=\"197\" />\n</p><p>The coefficient of the highest degree term becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/7/4c7256c8126fcd4acc3fc91fc241882edbd015cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p>\n<ul><li>Secondly, we suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is even, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/f/befdd410363e706de4f0fc61310abccc0a5d566a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan nx = \\dfrac{a_1\\tan x + a_3\\tan^3 x + \\cdots + a_{n - 1}\\tan^{n - 1} x}{a_0 + a_2\\tan^2 x + \\cdots + a_n\\tan^n x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"400\" height=\"44\" />, then</li></ul>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/9/0f9af737db28b97673f67d74e5ee6992db6f8bb1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\tan(n + 1)x &amp;= \\dfrac{\\tan nx + \\tan x}{1 - \\tan nx \\tan x}\\\\ &amp;= \\dfrac{\\dfrac{a_1\\tan x + a_3\\tan^3 x + \\cdots + a_{n - 1}\\tan^{n - 1} x}{a_0 + a_2\\tan^2 x + \\cdots + a_n\\tan^n x} + \\tan x}{1 - \\dfrac{a_1\\tan x + a_3\\tan^3 x + \\cdots + a_{n - 1}\\tan^{n - 1} x}{a_0 + a_2\\tan^2 x + \\cdots + a_n\\tan^n x}\\tan x}\\\\ &amp;= \\dfrac{a_1\\tan x + a_3\\tan^3 x + \\cdots + a_{n - 1}\\tan^{n - 1} x + a_0\\tan x + a_2\\tan^3 x + \\cdots \\boxed{+ a_n\\tan^{n + 1} x}}{a_0 + a_2\\tan^2 x + \\cdots + a_n\\tan^n x - a_1\\tan^2 x - a_3\\tan^4 x - \\cdots - a_{n - 1}\\tan^n x} \\end{align*}\" width=\"769\" height=\"191\" />\nThe coefficient of the highest degree term remains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1a2b6b7c193f9ba2b2134a59f1da5addcfbc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/6/c766f9fce6070981e62f805a7cf7294baed4498e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/9/559d5d5764d45ded08233db4c6e2db387af2ee84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />. During the process of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> increasing to 2023, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1a2b6b7c193f9ba2b2134a59f1da5addcfbc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> changed its sign a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/f/bdf425a048ad19cd876aa39b0277773a41610f22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2022 \\div 2 = 1011$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"130\" height=\"15\" /> times.\n</p><p>Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/2/242e7f2e317cf060eda0c332cad8adc4051c945b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2023} = 1 \\times (-1)^{1011} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"254\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Reda_mandymath\">reda_mandymath</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.282_minutes.2C_easy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(2_minutes,_easy)\">Solution 5 (2 minutes, easy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (2 minutes, easy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/3/793a43558562b093280c907471b8fc6f659668ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan 2x = \\dfrac{2 \\tan x}{1 - \\tan^2 x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"157\" height=\"40\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/5/8156b2f3620b7bb0a635d9fd1b412c9d075768bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan 3x = \\dfrac{3 \\tan x - \\tan^3 x}{1-3 \\tan^2 x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"200\" height=\"43\" />\nSince this is the AMC, conjecture that some pattern is to be found within the last term of the expansion of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/e/adefb12ecf6435096f44a582b5b55d1bdc60756e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan nx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />.\nGuess that the sign of the last term alternates between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/c/77cf26be132ef93923e082ee4153b2cb0ef44a50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$+$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add22d9bda21e86390bc74fa4dde17730a442da7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Indeed, for odd coefficients the last term has a negative sign, so choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/f/fffe39c557056d4c453fcaa390353f97488fc630.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"73\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~pixelpyguy\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution 1 by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/4KJR_1Kg4A4\">https://youtu.be/4KJR_1Kg4A4</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/0KH554CLayE\">https://youtu.be/0KH554CLayE</a>\n</p><p>~Steven Chen (Professor Chen Education Palace, www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A\">2023 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_